I remember getting very upset while loosing promising characters due 
to crashes back with nh_1.4f (DOS). The minute I got my hands on the
famous GameWizard I started playing Nethack inside it! - I didn't
*save*-scum but *memory*-scum.  ;-) Every time I was up to leaving a
level I stored a memory-image. So I got my first 'ascension' with (if
I recall correctly) 1 crash-restore. I didn't use this method to 
recover after dying, though...

Of course I played sometimes just for fun fixing some stats and
recover if something didn't work well enough. But that has *nothing*
to do with *playing* Nethack.

Later on (when Nethack got its own restore and was becoming more
stable) I dropped my GameWizard method. I never was really happy with
that kind of bending the character of the game. But I couldn't stand
to loose forever only due to crashes, either. Btw.: Although I tried 
later a couple of times I *always* run into a crash with nh_1.4f 
before ascension. :-(

